# Settings System

Dokan Kits implements a flexible settings system for storing and retrieving plugin configuration.

## Core Settings Files

- [includes/Core/Data/Models/Settings.php](mdc:includes/Core/Data/Models/Settings.php): Settings model class
- [includes/Core/Data/Stores/SettingsDataStore.php](mdc:includes/Core/Data/Stores/SettingsDataStore.php): Data store for settings

## Helper Functions

The plugin provides several helper functions for working with settings:

```php
// Get a setting
$setting = dokan_kits_get_setting('setting-name');

// Get a setting value
$value = dokan_kits_get_setting_value('setting-name', 'key', 'default-value');

// Update a setting
dokan_kits_update_setting('setting-name', 'value', 'new-value');

// Update multiple properties
dokan_kits_update_setting('setting-name', [
    'key1' => 'value1',
    'key2' => 'value2',
]);

// Delete a setting
dokan_kits_delete_setting('setting-name');
```

## Settings Structure

Settings are stored as key-value pairs with additional metadata:

- **name**: Unique identifier for the setting
- **value**: The actual setting value (can be scalar or array)
- **default**: Default value if not set
- **created_at**: When the setting was created
- **updated_at**: When the setting was last updated

## Admin Settings UI

The admin settings interface is built with React and can be found in:

- [src/admin/pages/dashboard/](mdc:src/admin/pages/dashboard): Admin dashboard pages
- [src/admin/components/fields/](mdc:src/admin/components/fields): Form field components
